WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.390
One person boards a plane to start
a new job in another country.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.610
Another family crosses
a sea in a small boat,

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.530
escaping danger at home.

4
00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.090
Both cross an international border.

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.850
Some moves add up.

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:20.570
In 2024, the UK was home to about
1.04 million people born in India.

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.290
So what pushes people to leave home,
and what pulls them somewhere new?

8
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:26.870
Is it mostly money?

9
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.070
Mostly war?

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.350
Mostly family?

11
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.150
In this mission, you'll sort
push factors from pull factors,

12
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.230
and draw them as arrows
between two places.

13
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.890
Then you'll learn how a refugee
differs from an economic migrant.

14
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.530
Your mission: find out what
pushes people to leave home,

15
00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.450
and what pulls them to a new one.
